xCobaCache /: xCobaCache::usage = "xCobaCache[lhs, rhs] checks whether there \
is a value in the xCobaCacheTable assigned to lhs, and returns it if there \
is. Otherwise the value rhs is stored in the cache, assigned to lhs, and \
returned. xCobaCache[lhs, rhs, name] stores the pair {lhs, rhs} with the \
given name, with default being the head of the expresion lhs. xCoba[lhs, rhs, \
name, simp] uses the simplification function simp on the rhs expression \
before storing it in the cache table."
 
